## Evidence by numbered outcome

1. Package skeleton. Cargo.toml:1 declares one explicit edition-2024 package,
   bboxy450-harness, with no workspace or inherited fields. It declares
   default=[], standalone, embedded and acp, and pins crates.io bboxy450-rt
   and bboxy450-yarn to 0.1.1. Every Rust source has the exact six-line
   ATTRIBUTION.md header; scripts/checks.py enforces it. The skeleton was signed
   and pushed first (364b92a after the authorized rebase).

2. Protocol. src/protocol/mod.rs:713 exports the schemars schema;
   protocol.schema.json is checked against it. tests/protocol_golden.rs:295
   checks exact round trips and forward-compatible unknown variants. Five
   JSONL fixtures cover text/reasoning, parallel reads, FileChange, Terminal,
   Plan, Approval, mid-tool interruption, recovery, Lagged and Reset.
   src/protocol/laws.rs:23 checks durable order, epochs, lifecycle, nested item
   closure and tool pairing; tests/protocol_laws.rs supplies broken controls.
   The protocol/fixtures were pushed early at e438e2e for the GUI consumer.
   The later ICD clarifications were cherry-picked from the Architect's signed
   commits, including async loading, compaction, forks and escaped digest fields.

3. Engine and other core components.

   - src/engine/mod.rs:37 owns configuration and the session actor. Work is
     bounded at 64; control has its separate 256-entry FIFO; recent op memory is
     1024. Bounded work batches preserve completion/control progress. Steer
     fallback retains admission order. src/engine/turn_loop.rs:35 supplies one
     production Yarn reactor topology, also projected by the formal test.
     Cancellation, child joins, synthetic tool results and the single ending
     are in turn_loop.rs:126 and task_group.rs:10. process.rs:43 owns its born
     process group, TERM/KILL, pipe drains and leader reaping.
   - src/provider/parser.rs:25 strictly assembles indexed streamed calls and
     rejects changed identities, duplicate ids, missing/conflicting finish
     markers and malformed arguments. provider/mod.rs:143 implements cancellable
     OpenAI-compatible HTTP, pre-output-only retry and Retry-After. Identical
     empty/repeated final metadata is accepted and covered by a regression.
     profile.rs resolves !cmd keys with an 8 KiB cap and 10 s timeout via the
     toolkit CommandRunner; Keychain commands are refused unattended.
   - src/tools.rs:174 implements read/write/edit/apply_patch/exec/bash/grep/glob,
     effect permits, four parallel reads, exclusive exec and per-path write
     locks. Exact edit misses give suggestions; apply_patch stages changes;
     output caps spill to scrubbed blobs. policy.rs:76 evaluates data rules with
     unattended deny. Every non-read effect has a recorded Approval resolution.
   - src/store.rs:210 writes durable JSONL before publication and fsyncs turn,
     approval and close boundaries. :261 recovers inner items before parents,
     synthesizes missing tool results and closes turns in a new epoch. The log
     itself holds the writer lease. Blobs are content-addressed and verified.
   - src/gateway/host.rs:39/:106 create or load/recover before exposing InProc.
     Subscribe never loads. Same-op creation is idempotent; a bound gateway
     refuses StartSession. Tests prove recovery-before-Hello, closed/missing/
     corrupt refusals, a failure Notice on the next successful open, and socket
     binding only after loading. gateway/mod.rs:266 coalesces deltas before
     copying growing bodies; snapshots are scrubbed again after assembly.
     Registration precedes lazy replay; slow readers get Lagged while healthy
     peers continue. gateway/unix.rs uses mode 0600, peer uid checks, bounded
     JSONL frames, correlated replies and a five-second unknown-outcome timeout.
     Idle clients receive Status every 15 seconds.
   - frontends/headless.rs:43 emits envelopes for -p/--json, and replays closed
     logs read-only without credentials or epoch mutation. seat.rs:90 streams
     append-only prefixes without duplicate final text or terminal controls.
     Signals are installed before key resolution; EOF/HUP/TERM cancel and join.
     Idle SetProfile resolves off the actor, so Close can cancel/join it; stale
     profile completions have no effect.
   - context/compact.rs:45 implements protocol section 4b's deterministic
     Markdown digest: clip then escape, omit unstarted turns/private bodies,
     drop oldest whole turns to 32 KiB, and retain the omission count. The blob
     is fsynced before completion. context/mod.rs:23 replaces old request items
     with one summary message and includes it in stable_prefix. The log stays
     intact. tests/context_compact.rs covers the golden, deterministic hash,
     prefix exclusion, repeated Compact refusal, cap and header injection.
   - store/fork.rs:88 materializes a quiescent parent prefix and every typed
     blob reference. Hash-checked blobs precede a fsynced temporary log and
     exclusive atomic rename. Child seq/event/timestamp/cause are retained;
     session/epoch are rewritten. tests/store_fork.rs proves exact copying
     during parent appends, unchanged parent bytes, BadFork refusals, no child
     publication on blob corruption, independence after parent deletion and
     equivalence of actual first ModelRequests.

4. Formal verification. Uses published bboxy450-tlc =0.1.1 and Yarn 0.1.1;
   there is no checker fork. AgentTurnLifecycle/ToolPairing map to the
   HarnessTurnLifecycle and HarnessTurnLifecyclePairing families. Other
   families cover A-B-A birth fencing/group kill, SteerQueue, approval races/
   unattended resolution, replay/register/lag/healthy-peer progress, dirty wake,
   profile retirement and atomic fork publication. All have failing Broken
   controls. tests/reactor_projection.rs checks every one of 15 nonempty
   readiness masks against the production declaration.

   verification/coverage.toml inventories the sole crate and every Rust source;
   corpus.toml independently fixes expected verdicts; contracts.toml maps
   sources, assumptions and real API/process witnesses. R20 compaction and R21
   fork implementation coverage are explicit. scripts/formal.py:73 rejects
   omissions, partial exploration, tool failure or disagreement. Java TLC 1.7.4
   and Temurin 21.0.13+9 are checksum-pinned; Java is never a runtime dependency.
   Receipt archives under verification/evidence/<digest>/ survive target cleanup.

   Bounds include two turns/tools, three birth generations, finite work/replay
   abstractions, one pending profile and a fixed fork point with two parent
   heads. Weak fairness applies only to named action groups. Fork crashes may
   repeat forever, so its model makes a safety claim, not a progress claim.
   No arbitrary Rust refinement or complete TLC replacement is claimed.

5. Live smoke. frontends/smoke.rs:25 uses exactly the requested Nemotron free
   model and OpenRouter endpoint. It copies only the kittens !cmd source into
   the local mode-0600 harness profile, never its output value. Only read/edit
   are allowed, and all rounds/retries share a three-request budget. The latest
   invocation passed with one read and one edit. Only the redacted summary is
   retained; its temporary real transcript is checked and removed. SKIP (no
   key) and UNAVAILABLE (quota) remain distinct from PASS.

## Failures and disposition

An early full run failed when parallel Java TLC processes shared temporary
standard-module files (Java exit 150). 26c82bf isolates them and adds a gate
negative control; later full parity runs pass. A later firehose run timed out:
1fffe52 coalesces before cloning partial bodies and skips unnecessary serde
round trips for an empty redaction set; the unchanged 100k-delta test passes.

One full run at 1fffe52 missed the profile-close two-second bound. Its captured
output/command results are retained in test-profile-timeout.log/.json. The
isolated test passed twelve fresh-process repetitions, including a private
HOME/TMPDIR. No product root cause was established from that older failure.
e47a3e0 strengthens the witness: the ready file follows child creation, it
observes SessionClosed directly at the unchanged two-second bound, reports
live-group/event diagnostics, and cleans its owned group on failure. The final
canonical run passes. The earlier failure is not relabeled as PASS.

The live summary retains three early failed one-request diagnostic invocations
and the previous three-request PASS; the latest PASS uses three more requests
(nine across development, at most three per invocation). Early failures exposed
the strict final-metadata parser issue; no failed attempt is counted as PASS.

## Deliberate scope and evidence limits

GUI/window/widgets, upstream workspace membership and embedded R15 toolkit
crate deduplication belong to other assignments. MCP is optional and omitted;
the ACP adapter is not implemented by this core task. No merge, crate release,
installation or deployment was performed. Automatic context compaction is
explicitly deferred by protocol section 4b.

Real HTTP/UTF-8 parsing, filesystem behavior, process groups, wall-clock bounds,
secret scrubbing and terminal bytes remain implementation witnesses. Finite
models do not prove those effects or GUI pixels. Tests use mock localhost SSE,
throwaway identities and real subprocesses/PTYs; none needs operator input.

U1-U7 interim mechanisms follow upstream-toolkit.md: credited local exporter and
metadata (U1), copied helpers with const variable counts (U2), standalone source
inventory rather than embedded integration (U3), local model shapes (U4), renamed
Yarn projection plus a separate fair semantic model (U5), name tables (U6), and
one local scoped JoinSet/cancellation group marked for upstream replacement (U7).

All product, tests and this report are signed and pushed on e1-core. Generated
formal archives remain local untracked run artifacts; product/test sources are
clean. The task report gives the exact final head, PR and refreshed receipt.
The Oracle must inspect the tree/diff and rerun the gates before accepting.
